{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And he was there.</b> Many thought that Moses stood on the mountain eighty days until HaShem gave him the tablets, and they did not speak correctly. Only the words of the ancients, of blessed memory, are true, as I have already mentioned: Moses stood on the mountain forty days until HaShem gave him the first tablets, and so it is written, “And Moses was on the mountain forty days and forty nights” (above 24:18), and it says, “And I fell down before HaShem the forty days and the forty nights” (Deuteronomy 9:25). Then Moses said the passage beginning “See, You say to me” (above 33:12), and afterward he went down and shattered the tablets, and went up with him onto Mount Sinai. And behold, it is written, “And YHWH passed before him” (above 34:6), and afterward, “And he was there with YHWH forty days and forty nights; bread he did not eat” — like its manner the first time, so also the second." "<b>And He wrote on the tablets.</b> HaShem wrote them, for so it is written: “And I will write on the tablets the words that were on the first tablets, which you shattered” (above 34:1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Resolved למעלה פ' ו as a reference to Exodus 34:6 (chapter 34, verse 6)."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:29.249910861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}